# Quality and Git

Follow `docs/project/CONSTITUTION.md` §§14–18, 20. Definition of Done is in §18.

## Validate with commands that exist

- `php artisan test` or `composer test`
- `php artisan route:list` after route changes
- `npx vite build` after frontend changes — **not** `npm run build`
- Isolated sqlite migrate for migration-risk work only

Do not invent scripts. Pint MAY run (`vendor/bin/pint`); there is no `pint.json`. No ESLint/Prettier.

Existing failures MUST be reported honestly (FileManager restore/forceDelete; `ExampleTest` GET `/`). Do not delete or hollow out tests to go green.

A Vue page rendering is not done. New mutating/admin endpoints need server-side authz, validation, and tests.

## Git

This repo already exists — never `git init`. Work on purpose-specific branches (`feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `docs/`, `refactor/`, `test/`). Inspect `git status` and `git diff` before commit. Keep commits scoped; do not mix unrelated work.

**Never push, force-push, skip hooks, or rewrite shared history** unless the user explicitly instructs it. Never commit `.env` or secrets. Do not create exploratory commits.
